  "body": "## Problem\n\nPR #3890 (#3888) refuses a Ramp or Helix entry or level transition under control or wear compensation, because those moves reach the wall before G41/G42 engages. The same PR notes an open gap: the Plunge and Arc entries also move under G40 before compensation engages. Nobody tested them against a register larger than the nominal radius, or a positive wear value.\n\nIf one of those moves can reach the finished wall before compensation is active, the program cuts the wall silently. That is the same class of defect as #3888.\n\n## Check and fix\n\n- For control and wear compensation, find each move between the end of the rapid and the first move with G41/G42 active, for each entry type (Plunge, Arc, Ramp, Helix) and each side (wall side, bore side).\n- Prove from the posted G-code that each such move stays at least the maximum allowed register difference away from the finished wall. Or move the compensation engage before it, or refuse the combination by name.\n- Pins on the posted G-code, with an oversized register and a positive wear value: the finished wall is not touched before G41/G42 is active.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Follow-up from PR #3890 (#3888) and the post-merge safety read of #3833.\n",
